Just so, hence the requirement that the connectives be taken as connecting =
only=20
atomic expressions, i.e., not grouped ones.  That's a hard rule to justify=
=20
within Lojban, but it works fine in Logic (Skolem normal forms), where the=
=20
negations are not part of the connective.  Of course, then, the 'ji' trick=
=20
doesn't work exactly.  On the other hand, using the groupings does cover so=
me=20
cases that simple normal forms don't -- that is, more that one TT line at o=
nce.



